<title>INDIA: START OF INDIA'S UNITED FRONT MEETING DELAYED.</title>
<headline>START OF INDIA'S UNITED FRONT MEETING DELAYED.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A meeting of India's ruling United Front decision-making Steering Committee to discuss oil prices was delayed, but it was still expected to take place on Wednesday evening, officials said.</p>
<p>The meeting, which would follow a gathering of the alliance's &quot;core committee&quot; earlier in the evening, had been scheduled to start at 7 p.m. (1330 GMT).</p>
<p>But Prime Minister Inder Kumar Gujral was held up by a separate meeting with parliamentarians and had still not reached the site of the Steering Committee meeting by 8:10 p.m. (1440 GMT), alliance officials said.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi Newsroom (91) 11-301-2024; Fax (91) 11-301-4043</p>
